# Copy to `.env.production` on the instance and fill in. Never commit the copy.
#
#     cp deploy/oci/.env.production.example deploy/oci/.env.production
#     chmod 600 deploy/oci/.env.production
#
# `.env.*` is already gitignored at the repository root, so the copy cannot be
# committed by accident. Nothing here reaches an image: the Dockerfiles carry
# no configuration and `backend/.dockerignore` keeps `.env` files out of the
# build context entirely.
#
# Every value below is read by `docker-compose.prod.yml`, which composes the
# four variables the backend actually validates -- DATABASE_URL,
# SYNC_DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL and CORS_ORIGINS -- from them. That indirection
# is deliberate: the database password is written once, not three times, so
# the two connection strings cannot drift apart.

# --- the public name ---------------------------------------------------------
# The hostname the browser uses, with no scheme and no trailing slash. Its DNS
# A record (and AAAA, if you assign an IPv6 address) must already point at this
# instance's public IP before the stack is started, or Caddy's certificate
# request fails and the site serves nothing.
#
# This is also what becomes CORS_ORIGINS=https://<this> for the API.
NOEMA_DOMAIN=

# Where Let's Encrypt sends expiry warnings. A real address you read.
ACME_EMAIL=

# --- the database ------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by the Postgres container to create the role and database on first
# start, and by the two connection strings the API and worker are given.
#
# Generate the password rather than choosing one, and do it on the instance:
#     openssl rand -base64 36 | tr -d '\n/+=' | cut -c1-40
#
# It is only ever sent over the compose network between containers on one
# host, never over the internet: the database publishes no host port.
POSTGRES_USER=noema
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=noema

# --- the release -------------------------------------------------------------
# Tags the built images so `docker image ls` says which commit is running and
# a rollback has something to name. Set it to the short commit SHA:
#     export NOEMA_VERSION=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)
# Left unset it becomes `dev`, which is fine for a first bring-up and useless
# afterwards.
NOEMA_VERSION=
